# No vendor document is committed. Datasheets, user manuals, board design
# packages and the chassis CAD are copyrighted and not ours to redistribute,
# so the repository records the vendor and the exact title of each one and
# nothing else - bom/README.md owns that record. On a fresh clone these files
# are absent and have to be fetched by hand.
/vendor/

# Written by mechanical/scripts/make-assembly.py, which works inside mechanical/cad/,
# so both files sit there rather than under vendor/. Ignored for
# size and churn, not for copyright.
#   assembly.stl              pure output - delete it and re-run
#   chassis-3deck-fascia.obj  a SEED the script rewrites in place. It is not
#                             reproducible from the script alone; it started as
#                             a Rhino export of the .3dm. Back it up locally.
mechanical/cad/assembly.stl
mechanical/cad/chassis-3deck-fascia.obj

# fascia-lower.stl and fascia-upper.stl are tracked on purpose: OpenSCAD output
# shifts between versions, and these are the files that actually went to the
# printer.

# Written by mechanical/scripts/plate1.py and make-assembly.py - pure output, re-run them.
mechanical/cad/plate1/
mechanical/cad/chassis-3deck-fascia.mtl

# Videos and stills, written by mechanical/scripts/animate-*.py - pure output.
mechanical/renders/

# Python bytecode, from importing hardware/stm32-carrier.py
__pycache__/
